<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luo River (Henan)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Luo River is a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, flowing about 450 kilometres from the Qinling mountains past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>. Its valley was a heartland of early Chinese civilisation, and Luoyang, the royal capital of the Eastern Zhou, takes its name from it. The river joins the Yellow River near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongyi">Gongyi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luo-river-henan.jpg" alt="Luo River (Henan)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Potatohai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luo_River_Luoyang.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
